  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet the boost/charge-pump input decoupling capacitor C1 is drawn as 0.1 µF / 16 V (sitting on the Display_Power_Switch rail to GND, alongside C2 = 1 µF / 6.3 V).",
      "expected": "The specification's EPD-driver matching table lists C1 in the 'default 1 µF / 25 V' group (C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V), i.e. the intended part is 1 µF / 25 V. The build's C1 is 10× smaller in capacitance and rated 16 V instead of 25 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C1 0.1uF/16V  (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch, left of L1/C2 on the Display_Power_Switch node)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default (EPD_Driver vs PDI reference table, §4)"}
      ],
      "impact": "C1 is the bulk decoupling capacitor on the EPD power-switch rail that feeds the boost converter (L1) and the panel VDD/VDDIO. Replacing the intended 1 µF with 0.1 µF removes most of the charge reservoir on that rail, so during boost switching the rail can sag, causing e-paper refresh glitches or failed panel power-up; the 16 V rating is also below the 25 V called for by the reference design.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the board matches the specification (FAN53610 power stage, barrel-jack battery disconnect, Q2 high-side EPD switch, EPD signal mapping, keyboard matrix, debug UART). The one clear deviation from the intended design is C1 on the EPD_Driver sheet, drawn as 0.1 µF/16 V where the spec's component-matching table requires 1 µF/25 V, a value/rating error on the EPD boost-rail decoupling capacitor."
}

